  "id": "COMPOUND:23096 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) is implicated in the regulation of VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-hydroxy-6,8-dimethoxy-2,3-dimethylbenzo[G]chromen-4-one and tetraethylammonium. These compounds all ultimately target VMRC-MELG, indicating a shared mechanism of action involving the modulation of a common downstream effector. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) in influencing VMRC-MELG through a network of targets that may converge on this final effector. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound exerts its biological effect via a series of intermediate targets, ultimately leading to the regulation of VMRC-MELG.",
